$DATUM 67-63-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Hydrazination of 1,5-diketones 1a and 1b ( general procedure ). A
solution of 3 mmol of 1,5-diketone 1a or 1b in 30 mL of propan-2-ol was
heated to 80°C, 12 mmol of hydrazine hydrate was added, and the mixture
was kept for 24 h. The precipitate was filtered off and washed with
water. Recrystallization from propan-2-ol gave compound 2, and compound 3
was isolated by evaporation of the filtrate. The oily material obtained
in the reaction with 1b was treated with diisopropyl ether, and
subsequent recrystallization from propan-2-ol afforded diazepine 4.
1-Phenyl-2-(3-phenyl-3,3a,4,5-tetrahydro-2H-benzo[
g]indazol-3-yl)ethanone (2). Yield 30%, colorless crystals.
2-(3,5-Diphenyl-3,4-dihydro-2H-pyrazol-3-yl)-3,4-dihydronaphthalen-1-amine
(3). Yield 15%, colorless crystals. 2: mp 189-190°C (from i-PrOH). IR
spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3302-3448 br (NH), 3025-3048 (C-Harom), 2930
(C-Haliph), 1690 (C=O), 1660 (C=N), 1444-1607 (C=Carom). 1H NMR spectrum,
δ, ppm: 1.84-1.94 m (2H, CH2), 2.72-2.98 m (2H, CH2), 3.22 q (1H, CH, J =
4.8 Hz), 3.63 d and 4.50 d (1H each, 1′-H, J = 18 Hz), 7.04 s (NH),
7.14-7.92 m (14H, Harom). 13C NMR spectrum, δC, ppm: 23.80 (C4), 29.82
(C5), 48.42 (C1′'), 55.04 (C3), 72.72 (C3a), 124.32-137.64 (Carom),
140.64 (C9b), 197.34 (C2′). Found, %: C 82.27; H 6.39; N 7.68. C25H22N2O.
Calculated, %: C 81.94; H 6.05; N 7.64. 3: mp 198-199°C (from EtOH). IR
spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3133 (NH2), 1683 (C=N), 1590 (C=C). 1H NMR spectrum,
δ, ppm: 2.04 s and 2.12 s (1H each, 4′-H), 2.94-3.34 m (4H, CH2), 4.04 s
(2H, NH2), 4.24 s (1H, NH). Found, %: C 82.83; H 6.43; N 11.81. C25H23N3.
Calculated, %: C 82.16; H 6.34; N 11.50.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
